# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../doc/files.rst:301
msgid ""
"When you use :guilabel:`Link to Existing...`, OpenShot tries to match each "
"selected source clip to an existing optimized file in a safe order. It first"
" looks for the same base filename with a different video extension, then for"
" common proxy-style names such as ``_proxy``, ``_preview``, ``_optimized``, "
"``_lowres``, resolution tags such as ``_720p`` or ``_1080p``, and "
"camera/editor-style variants such as ``_p``. It also supports names that add"
" the OpenShot file ID after a known proxy suffix, such as "
"``clip001_proxy_F1.mp4``, and it can still match files named only by file "
"ID, such as ``F1.mp4``."
msgstr ""
"Saat Anda menggunakan :guilabel:`Tautkan ke yang Ada...`, OpenShot mencoba "
"mencocokkan setiap klip sumber yang dipilih dengan file yang dioptimalkan "
"yang sudah ada dalam urutan yang aman. Pertama mencari nama file dasar yang "
"sama dengan ekstensi video berbeda, kemudian nama gaya proxy umum seperti "
"``_proxy``, ``_preview``, ``_optimized``, ``_lowres``, tag resolusi seperti "
"``_720p`` atau ``_1080p``, dan varian gaya kamera/editor seperti ``_p``. Ini"
" juga mendukung nama yang menambahkan ID file OpenShot setelah akhiran proxy"
" yang dikenal, seperti ``clip001_proxy_F1.mp4``, dan masih bisa mencocokkan "
"file yang hanya dinamai dengan ID file, seperti ``F1.mp4``."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../doc/files.rst:308
msgid ""
"Best practice when bringing your own optimized files is to keep the same "
"base filename as the source clip and add a clear proxy-style suffix, for "
"example ``clip001_proxy.mp4`` or ``clip001_proxy.mov``. If you need to avoid"
" filename collisions, append the OpenShot file ID after the proxy suffix, "
"for example ``clip001_proxy_F1.mp4``. Avoid unrelated suffixes such as "
"``_final`` or ``_reviewcopy``, because OpenShot does not treat those as safe"
" proxy naming patterns."
msgstr ""
"Praktik terbaik saat membawa file yang dioptimalkan sendiri adalah menjaga "
"nama file dasar yang sama dengan klip sumber dan menambahkan akhiran gaya "
"proxy yang jelas, misalnya ``clip001_proxy.mp4`` atau ``clip001_proxy.mov``."
" Jika Anda perlu menghindari tabrakan nama file, tambahkan ID file OpenShot "
"setelah akhiran proxy, misalnya ``clip001_proxy_F1.mp4``. Hindari akhiran "
"yang tidak terkait seperti ``_final`` atau ``_reviewcopy``, karena OpenShot "
"tidak menganggapnya sebagai pola penamaan proxy yang aman."

#: ../doc/files.rst:317
msgid ""
"Use **Split File** to choose the parts of a longer recording you want to "
"work with. Right click a file in **Project Files** and choose "
":guilabel:`Split File`. Select the start and end of a segment, give it an "
"optional name, and click :guilabel:`Create`. Adjust the markers and repeat "
"to prepare as many segments as you need."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan **Split File** untuk memilih bagian dari rekaman panjang yang ingin "
"Anda kerjakan. Klik kanan file di **Project Files** dan pilih "
":guilabel:`Split File`. Pilih awal dan akhir segmen, beri nama opsional, dan"
" klik :guilabel:`Create`. Sesuaikan penanda dan ulangi untuk menyiapkan "
"sebanyak segmen yang Anda butuhkan."

#: ../doc/files.rst:322
msgid ""
"Each segment appears in Project Files and can be added to the timeline like "
"any other file. The segments all use the original media on disk, so you can "
"prepare them without making extra copies of the recording."
msgstr ""
"Setiap segmen muncul di Project Files dan dapat ditambahkan ke timeline "
"seperti file lainnya. Semua segmen menggunakan media asli di disk, jadi Anda"
" dapat menyiapkannya tanpa membuat salinan tambahan dari rekaman."

#: ../doc/files.rst:325
msgid ""
"When you add a segment to the timeline, OpenShot gives its properties "
"starting keyframes at the segment's beginning. For example, with "
":ref:`auto_keyframes_ref` on, you can move to the end and change the "
"rotation to make it turn over the length of that segment. The animation "
"starts from the part you chose to use."
msgstr ""
"Saat Anda menambahkan segmen ke timeline, OpenShot memberikan properti "
"dengan keyframe awal di awal segmen. Misalnya, dengan "
":ref:`auto_keyframes_ref` aktif, Anda dapat bergerak ke akhir dan mengubah "
"rotasi untuk membuatnya berputar sepanjang segmen tersebut. Animasi dimulai "
"dari bagian yang Anda pilih untuk digunakan."

#: ../doc/files.rst:329
msgid ""
"If you have already animated a timeline clip, slicing it preserves that "
"animation through the cut. Split File is useful for choosing your segments "
"before you begin that work."
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda sudah menganimasikan klip timeline, memotongnya mempertahankan "
"animasi tersebut melalui pemotongan. Split File berguna untuk memilih segmen"
" Anda sebelum memulai pekerjaan tersebut."

#: ../doc/files.rst:332
msgid ""
"Preview an existing split-file entry to adjust its saved IN/OUT range. The "
"ruler includes the surrounding footage, allowing you to extend the range "
"again without reimporting the source."
msgstr ""
"Pratinjau entri split-file yang ada untuk menyesuaikan rentang IN/OUT yang "
"disimpan. Penggaris mencakup rekaman di sekitarnya, memungkinkan Anda "
"memperpanjang rentang lagi tanpa mengimpor ulang sumber."

# Translated with gpt-4.1-mini
#: ../doc/files.rst:336
msgid ""
"Please refer to the section :ref:`clips_cutting_slicing_ref` for more ways "
"to cut and slice clips directly in the timeline."
msgstr ""
"Silakan lihat bagian :ref:`clips_cutting_slicing_ref` untuk cara lain "
"memotong dan membagi klip langsung di timeline."

